from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "What the Eye Cannot See"
AMBIENCE = "Night Crickets"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about how instruments gently extend our senses into worlds the bare eye can never reach.
SECTIONS = [['Let yourself settle now, somewhere soft and warm, where the day can finally fall away from you.', 'There is nothing here you need to do, nothing to solve, nothing to carry into this quiet hour.', 'Let these words drift down over you the way dusk drifts down over a still and darkening field.', 'You can let them blur and soften, the way a room softens when the last lamp is turned low.', 'Your breath is slow and easy now, rising and falling all on its own, asking nothing of you.', 'Feel how heavy your body has grown, sinking gently into whatever holds you in the dark.', 'Your shoulders loosen, your hands grow warm, and the small tightness behind your brow lets go.', 'And your eyes, those tired and faithful eyes, may close now, or simply grow heavy and dim.', 'Behind your closed eyelids there is a soft and private dark, and it is yours to rest in.', 'There is nothing to look at here, nothing to watch, only this warm and easy darkness.', 'Let each breath out carry a little more of the day away, until there is almost nothing left to hold.', 'Just breathe, and let the words carry you gently down toward sleep.'], ['Rest now in that soft dark, and let me tell you a quiet thing about the light you cannot see.', 'Your eyes are faithful and clever, but they catch only a thin ribbon of all the light there is.', 'Think of light as a long, long song, stretching out far past either end of what you can hear.', 'Your eyes hear only a small band of it, a narrow sliver of colours between red and violet.', 'Red at one soft edge, then orange, yellow, green, blue, and violet fading away at the other.', 'That whole rainbow, every colour you have ever seen, is only a sliver of the light around you.', 'Beyond the red, the light goes on, slower and longer, where your eyes can no longer follow.', 'Beyond the violet, it goes on too, faster and finer, into a brightness you have never glimpsed.', 'All of it is here now, in this room, passing through the dark, gentle and unseen.', 'You were never meant to see it all, and that is no loss, only a quiet and lovely mystery.', 'The world has always been larger than the small bright window of your eyes.', 'Let that thought settle softly over you, light as a blanket, and breathe.'], ['Long ago, people began, very gently, to build new eyes for the things they could not see.', 'In a quiet Dutch town in the sixteen seventies, a man named Antonie van Leeuwenhoek ground tiny lenses.', 'He was patient and curious, polishing little beads of glass no bigger than a drop of water.', 'One day he held up a single drop of still pond water, and he looked, and he was astonished.', 'For there, in that one small drop, a whole living world was swimming and turning in the light.', 'Tiny creatures, too small for any eye, drifting and spinning, alive and busy and uncounted.', 'He called them his little animalcules, his small animals, and no one had ever seen them before.', 'They had been there all along, in every pond and puddle and raindrop, humming with quiet life.', 'A single drop of water, it turned out, was as crowded and alive as a whole dark sea.', 'And all it took was a small clear lens, and a patient eye, and the willingness to look closely.', 'Imagine that hidden world, swimming softly even now in the still water of the night.', 'Let it drift through your mind, slow and luminous, as you sink a little deeper toward sleep.'], ['Others turned their small clear lenses the other way, away from the near and toward the far.', 'They built the telescope, a gentle eye for the faint and the distant, and lifted it to the sky.', 'And the dim, far things of the heavens were drawn gently close, the way a whisper is drawn near.', 'Stars too faint to see came softly into view, more and more of them, until the dark was full.', 'The blur of the night sky bloomed into countless distant suns, each one quietly burning alone.', 'Around far planets, small pale moons appeared, circling slowly in the dark, patient and unhurried.', 'All of it had been there always, glowing softly above, whether or not anyone was looking up.', 'The telescope did not make the stars; it only gathered their old, faint light and brought it near.', 'And the microscope did not make the little creatures; it only let a tired eye finally see them.', 'Each instrument was just a gentle extension of a human sense, patiently made by patient hands.', 'They never replaced the wonder; they only widened it, opening the small window a little more.', 'Breathe slowly now, and let the far stars and the near creatures drift together in the dark.'], ['In time, people grew bolder still, and built eyes for the very light their own eyes could never catch.', 'Beyond the red, in that slow and gentle light, lies the warm glow that living things give off.', 'It is called infrared, the soft light of warmth, and every warm thing quietly shines with it.', 'Your own body glows with it now, softly, in the dark, a warm and living light you cannot see.', 'A warm stone at evening shines with it; a sleeping creature glows; a hand leaves warmth behind.', 'With the right new eyes, the dark is not empty at all, but full of soft and living warmth.', 'And beyond the violet lies another light, finer and faster, called the ultraviolet.', 'Your eyes cannot see it, but the small bees can, and to them the flowers are not as they seem.', 'On petals that look plain to you, the bees see secret paths and patterns, lit up like gentle runways.', 'Signs painted in a light you cannot read, guiding them softly inward to the sweetness at the heart.', 'The flowers were never plain; they were only speaking in a colour your eyes were not made to hear.', 'Let that hidden warmth and that hidden colour glow quietly in your mind as you drift.'], ['There is more, softer and stranger still, in the long slow reaches beyond the warmth.', 'Far past the infrared lie the radio waves, the longest and gentlest light of all.', 'We built great quiet dishes, like cupped hands turned up to the sky, to listen for them.', 'And in that listening, we heard the faint hum of distant galaxies, whispering across the dark.', 'Light so old and so faint it left its far-off home before the earth was even here.', 'A soft, steady murmur from the edges of everything, gathered gently into our patient ears of metal.', 'And at the other far end, past the violet, lie the fine and searching x-rays.', 'They pass softly through the soft parts of you and are caught by the quiet bones within.', 'Hold up a hand to that unseen light, and there, gently, are the bones inside your living hand.', 'All these lights were here always, humming and glowing softly, long before anyone could sense them.', 'We did not invent them; we only, slowly, learned to listen, and the unseen world answered.', 'Let it all hum on around you now, gentle and vast, as you sink deeper into the warm dark.'], ['So let the seeing soften now, and let even the wondering grow slow and dim.', 'The whole unseen world is here around you still, humming softly, and it asks nothing of you.', 'The little creatures swim in their drop; the far galaxies whisper; the warm things glow in the dark.', 'It will all go on without you tonight, gentle and patient, as it always has and always will.', 'You do not have to sense it, or hold it, or understand it; you can simply let it hum on alone.', 'Your eyes are closed, and they may stay closed; there is no light here you need to catch.', 'Let your tired senses soften, one by one, and set themselves quietly down for the night.', 'There is no world to gather tonight, no hidden thing to seek, no faint light to listen for.', 'Only the warm dark, soft and complete, full of unseen things humming gently all around you.', 'Your breath grows slow, your body heavy, your thoughts thin and far away as distant stars.', 'Let the hidden world hum on without you, and let the quiet dark hold you, and let go.', 'Rest now, and drift, and sleep.']]
